Apertus 1.5's get_language_model() returns the inner ApertusModel, which has
.layers but no .model. Model runner v2's DSpark loader dereferences
target_language_model.model. Same fix as
serving/patches/vllm-apertus-dspark-mrv2-inner.patch, rebased on vLLM v0.31.0.

--- a/workspace/vllm/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/dspark/utils.py
+++ b/workspace/vllm/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/dspark/utils.py
@@ -111,7 +111,10 @@ def load_dspark_model(target_model: nn.Module, vllm_config: VllmConfig) -> nn.Mo
         if hasattr(target_model, "get_language_model")
         else target_model
     )
-    target_inner = target_language_model.model
+    # Apertus1p5ForConditionalGeneration.get_language_model() returns the
+    # inner ApertusModel (an EagleModelMixin with .layers), not a wrapper
+    # with .model. Use it directly in that case.
+    target_inner = getattr(target_language_model, "model", target_language_model)
     draft_inner = draft_model.model
     target_vocab_size = vllm_config.model_config.get_vocab_size()
 
